          deck: '62 cards (22 trumps + 40 suit cards). Low cards (1-4 Swords/Batons, 7-10 Cups/Coins) are removed.',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: "Dealer gets 17 cards, others 15 cards. The dealer discards 2 cards face-down (the 'Scarto').",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score 57 or more points from a pool of 114 available points.',
          gameplay: "Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite) play four deals anticlockwise. Each deal: dealer gives 15 cards to the player to his right, 15 to partner, 15 to the player to his left, and 17 to himself; dealer then discards two cards face-down (scarto). Player to dealer's right leads to the first trick. Follow suit if possible; if not, play a trump if possible; otherwise play any card. Trick with trumps is won by highest trump; trick without trumps by highest card of led suit. Winner of each trick leads to the next. The Fool may be played to any trick and never wins; it is added to the team of whoever played it. Team with more than 57 of the 114 points over the four deals wins the game.",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow suit if possible; if void in suit led, must play a trump if possible.',
            'Fool may be played to any trick; it never wins and is not captured; it counts for the team of the player who played it.',
            'Dealer may not discard 5-point cards (Kings, Trump 21, Trump 1, Fool).',
            '57 or more points of 114 wins a deal; team ahead on total points after four deals wins the game.',
            'Partners may communicate about their cards and tactics within defined limits (open communication).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize the protection of the 'Bagatto' (Trump 1). It is worth 5 points but is easily captured. Use the 'Matto' (Fool) to save a high card from a trick you know your partner will win anyway. If you are the dealer, discard useless low numbers into your 'Scarto' to ensure your team captures those 1-point cards early.",
          intermediate: "The 'Public Signal': When your partner leads a suit, if you have the King, tap the table once. This tells them they don't need to waste a Trump. If you have the Ace, you might use the code word 'Batto' to signal that you will take control of the round. Remember, the opponents hear this tooâ€”use it to intimidate them into playing their low trumps early.",
          advanced: "Trump Exhaustion: Because there are 21 trumps, you must track which ones have been played. If the 21 and 20 are gone, the 19 becomes the 'King' of the board. Coordination is key: if one partner has high trumps, the other should feed them 'Counters' (10s and face cards) to maximize the point yield from those winning tricks.",
          tips: [
            'If you win all tricks (Vola), the payout is doubled.',
            "Don't discard 5-point cards! It's illegal in most variants unless you have no other choice.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
