        prompts: {
          human: "Piedicavallo Tarocchi is a rare and highly localized variant of Italian Tarot played exclusively in the Valle Cervo of the Piedmont region. It uses a modified 62-card 'Tarocco Piemontese' deck. The game is famous for its 'Open Communication' system, where partners are legally allowed to speak to each other and signal their cards (using taps and code words) as long as the information is audible to the opponents. It is a game of deep tactical coordination, memory, and traditional heritage.",
